{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Replaces a text command's file-level import block (the impl record's `import` field) and recompiles. The one section patch_command_body cannot reach: `code_body` is a function body, so file-level `use`/import statements live here. Refuses flow commands. Returns the compile outcome plus old_imports. Preserves the impl record's existing readers/writers across the rewrite. JOURNALED on the control's patch journal (facet \"command\", cmd = the name, op \"imports\", old/new = the import blocks, compile ok|err), also when the compile fails; setting the same imports writes no entry. The result carries patch_id when an entry was written, or journal_warning when the edit landed but could not be journaled. label is the stated reason for the edit, recorded on the entry (the why-harvest pairs it with the change; empty is allowed and records no reason); an empty author defaults to the calling session's user, else anonymous.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::data;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse crate::dev::dev::compile::compile;","params":[{"name":"lib","type":"String"},{"name":"ctl","type":"String"},{"name":"cmd","type":"String"},{"name":"imports","type":"String"},{"desc":"The stated reason for this edit, recorded on the journal entry (the why-harvest pairs it with the change). May be empty, which records no reason.","name":"label","type":"String"},{"desc":"Who is making the edit, recorded on the journal entry. Empty defaults to the calling session's user, else anonymous.","name":"author","type":"String"},{"desc":"Request metadata filled in by the framework; pass an empty string from tools.","name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"opoush19fbdfbfefbn1","readers":[],"time":1794510433540,"username":"system","writers":[]}